{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfv1hwiXiRVUuExxobv2n","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote 259 tests in `tests/test_agent.py`, and they all pass with your venv's pytest. The library code is unchanged, and the tests use only pytest and the standard library.\n\n**What's covered:**\n- **Basic matching:** fixed, named and numbered fields; escaped `{{ }}`; regex special characters in plain text; case sensitivity on and off; newlines inside fields; the shortest possible match is taken.\n- **Field names:** dotted, hyphenated and bracketed names (which build nested dicts), name collisions like `a.b` / `a_b` / `a-b`, repeated names that must match the same value, and `RepeatedNameError` when they have different types.\n- **Integers:** `d` with automatic base detection (`0x`/`0b`/`0o`), signs, width limits, `,` and `_` grouping, `=` alignment; `n`, `b`, `o`, `x`/`X`; and `int_convert` called directly.\n- **Floats:** `f` (including nan/inf and `.0f`), `F` returning a Decimal, `e`, `g`, and `%`.\n- **Text types:** `w`, `W`, `s`, `S`, `D`, `l`, plus width and precision limits.\n- **Alignment and fill:** `<`, `>`, `^`, and fill characters that are special in regex.\n- **Format specs:** `extract_format` on its own, unknown types raising `ValueError`, and every allowed type compiling.\n- **Dates and times:** every built-in type (`ti`, `tg`, `ta`, `te`, `th`, `tc`, `tt`, `ts`), including AM/PM and the 12 AM/PM edge cases, timezone offsets in several formats, and microseconds; strftime-style specs returning a date, a datetime or a time; and `FixedTzOffset`.\n- **Custom types:** `extra_types`, `with_pattern`, and `regex_group_count`. Several tests check that fields after a type with extra internal regex groups still line up, which is where index-offset bugs would show.\n- **API surface:** `spans`, `search`/`findall` with `pos`/`endpos`, `evaluate_result=False` with `Match`, `compile`/`Parser` properties and repr, `Result`, more than 100 fields, pickling, and round-trips through `str.format`.\n\n**Fixes during the run:** six tests failed the first time. All six were wrong expectations on my part, not library bugs, and I corrected them:\n- A width like `{:5}` is a minimum length, so the captured text includes its padding.\n- `fixed_fields` holds regex group numbers, not positions in the format string.\n- `^` can't be used as a fill character because it's read as the alignment.\n- `{:d}` accepts a leading space as a sign.\n\nI also silenced one deprecation warning from Python's `strptime`. It comes from the test that parses a date with no year, which is exactly the behaviour that test is checking."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":521,"cache_read_input_tokens":55613,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":521},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"dbc1ca14-a45f-4106-a67e-34ab19ceda87","uuid":"880f36c0-c8b8-4681-8ca6-df21d55486f9","timestamp":"2026-10-11T06:56:19.410Z","request_id":"req_011Cfv1hwMSoT42T2y28xAUS"}
